<title>BELGIUM: Almanij surges on Gevaert, Cobepa deal.</title>
<headline>Almanij surges on Gevaert, Cobepa deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Belgian holding company Almanij surged to a new life high on Monday on news the group would acquire around half the portfolio of holding company Gevaert in a deal with Belgium's Cobepa group.</p>
<p>Under the deal, Almanij will carry out a 10-for-one stock split, offering a bonus share for every fifty held.</p>
<p>Around 0825 the shares were up 13.45 percent at 17,500 francs, a new life high. Cobepa shares were up more than six percent. Gevaert shares had not yet traded, but bid/ask prices were also marked sharply higher.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
